// applyZoomSafeViewportVars keeps --vw100/--dvh100 custom properties equal to
// the real, physical viewport size regardless of the uiZoom interface scale.
// CSS vw/vh/dvh units are specified to resolve against the true viewport -
// unlike percentage or auto-sized layout, they do NOT shrink to compensate
// for CSS `zoom` on <html> the way everything else in a zoomed subtree does.
// The release detail dialog (and its internal height math) used raw
// 100vw/100dvh, so at e.g. 110% zoom it rendered ~1.1x larger than the real
// window - clipping its rightmost action button and content off the edge
// with no way to reach it. Deriving these variables from
// window.innerWidth/innerHeight divided by the zoom factor, and using them
