let lastReplacementFinished='';
// downloadReplacementSeen gates whether a COMPLETED bulk delete/replace job
// is shown: the /jobs/download-replacements job record persists on the
// server indefinitely, so without this every visit to Download Activity
// would re-show the outcome of whatever such job last ran, potentially long
// ago (e.g. "Delete complete · 0 removed" forever after one empty run).
// Only a job that's actively running when we poll (genuinely in-progress,
// worth surfacing even on a fresh page load), or one WE just queued this
// page session (bulkDeleteDownloads sets this before polling), is allowed
// to show its completed status.
let downloadReplacementSeen=false;
